    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Trotsky formulated the theory of permanent revolution in 1905: in a backward country only the working class could overthrow feudalism, and it would then have to appeal to the workers of the advanced capitalist countries.</li><li>Trotskyists oppose Stalin's theory of socialism in one country and describe the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> after 1924 as a degenerated workers' state, ruled by a bureaucracy that suppressed democracy.</li><li>Trotsky was expelled from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> in 1929 and founded the Fourth International in 1938; he was attacked in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a> on 20 August 1940 by Ramón Mercader, an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nkvd">NKVD</a> agent, and died the next day.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The word Trotskyism was coined, according to Trotsky, by the Russian liberal leader Pavel Milyukov, who fought it &quot;as early as 1905&quot;; in 1917 Lenin's April Theses were themselves condemned by his opponents as Trotskyist.</p></aside>
    </section>

